  "comments": "<p>1939<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d7797bdbd80b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d7797bdbd80b.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>1949D<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637faa1e3f3c0.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637faa1e3f3c0.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>1954S<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637faa3c4d76f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637faa3c4d76f.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>1955D<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637faa4edde27.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637faa4edde27.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>1969S<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637faa6d5df90.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637faa6d5df90.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>1979S<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637faa8c479d9.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637faa8c479d9.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>1981S<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637faaa92efc6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637faaa92efc6.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>Mintage of this coin was stopped during World War II from 1942 to 1945 due to the need for nickel for the war effort. &nbsp;During those years a different alloy without nickel containing silver was used. &nbsp;War-time nickels are listed separately as KM#192a. &nbsp;The mintage of this coin resumed in 1946 as KM# A192.&nbsp;<br><br>1938 thru 1989 = 5 full steps<br>1990 to date = 6 full steps<br><br>From 1965 to 1967, these coins were minted in Philadelphia and Denver without a mintmark.<br><br>There are 1999 P and possibly other dates which exhibit DDD (Die Deterioration Doubling). These coins exhibit doubling, thickening, twisting and other deformities which results from die deterioration. Die deterioration is the result of die wear or improper heat treating (of the dies) combined with die wear.</p>",
